DOES ANY RECOMMENDED PRACTICE PREDICT RE-EXECUTION?
Trisovic et al. 2022 corpus. Unit = replication package. Cleaning condition,
symmetric combining rule. Outcome = the package has >=1 R file that ran.
============================================================================================
  2060 packages with at least one classifiable R file; 619 (30.0%) have one that ran.
  (The file-level rate over the same condition is 19.3%%; a package rate is
   higher because one success rescues the package. Both are in the record.)

  !! THE 'AT LEAST ONE FILE RAN' OUTCOME IS MECHANICALLY INFLATED BY PACKAGE
  SIZE: a package with 20 files has twenty chances. Measured below, that
  artifact is the single largest association in the whole table (z = +16.8),
  and it is a property of my outcome definition, not of the world. So the
  PRIMARY outcome here is the FILE-LEVEL rate within each group -- total
  files that ran over total files -- which cannot be inflated that way, with
  z divided by sqrt(design effect) for clustering.

